        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(release): reuse exact evidence across candidate deltas",
        "body": "Closes #103423\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nResolves a release-operations problem where small audited candidate deltas forced every broad release lane to restart, even when changed paths and package bytes could prove most prior evidence remained valid.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis adds a trusted-main, policy-driven terminal evidence workflow. It recomputes ancestry and path impact, binds reused and fresh proof to exact native run/job/artifact identities, validates package and ClawHub bytes, records complete cancelled-aggregate dispositions, and makes publish consumers revalidate live release state before any promotion. The workflow is validation-only and has no publication permissions.\n\n## User Impact\n\nRelease operators can rerun only gates affected by a candidate delta while retaining an immutable manifest with source/target SHAs, changed paths, artifact hashes, run IDs, conclusions, and explicit reuse rationale. Unchanged full-matrix evidence is reused only when the checked-in policy and exact artifact contracts prove it remains valid.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Frozen strict-v3 Testbox: core resolver/package suites 14/14; Telegram artifact attestation 1/1.\n- Install-smoke conflict proof: 65/65 focused tests after rebasing onto current `main`.\n- Static proof on exact head: Node and shell syntax, `actionlint`, docs MDX/link audit, formatting, and `git diff --check`.\n- Fresh exact-head combined Testbox, `check:changed`, autoreview, and hosted checks are running; this draft will be updated with terminal run IDs before review.\n\nAI-assisted implementation; all code, workflow contracts, and evidence are being reviewed and validated before landing.\n",
